     "created_at": "2023-06-09T02:28:50Z",
     "updated_at": "2023-06-09T02:28:50Z",
     "body": "I believe that it’s already supported. We can set slot.name directly in the connector configuration. Just like how we set `database.hostname` , `database.dbname` .\r\nThe debezium connector is based on the kafka debezium connector. For debezium-postgres-connecotor, it’s using PostgresConnectorTask .\r\nSo we can use the settings inherited from the kafka connector. Here is the documentation for `slot.name` :https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/connectors/postgresql.html#postgresql-property-slot-name",
     "author_association": "MEMBER",
